statement:
Let $k$ be a separably closed field and let $C$ be a smooth projective curve over $k$ [def-pc-smooth-projective-curve] which is geometrically integral [def-pc-geometrically-irreducible], of genus $g=\dim_kH^1(C,\mathcal O_C)$ [def-pc-genus]. For $d\in\mathbf Z$ let $\operatorname{Pic}^d_{C/k}$ be the subfunctor of the Picard functor $\operatorname{Pic}_{C/k}$ [def-pc-picard-functor] on $(\mathit{Sch}/k)_{fppf}$ of the classes whose fibrewise degree [def-pd-fibrewise-degree] is identically $d$. Let $d\geq0$, let $H_d$ be a $k$-scheme representing [def-pc-representable-functor] $\operatorname{Hilb}^d_{C/k}$ [def-pc-hilb-functor], let $D_d\subset H_d\times_kC$ be the universal closed subscheme (the element of $\operatorname{Hilb}^d_{C/k}(H_d)$ corresponding to $\mathrm{id}_{H_d}$), and let $P_d$ be a $k$-scheme representing $\operatorname{Pic}^d_{C/k}$. Then:

1. $D_d$ is a relative effective Cartier divisor on $H_d\times_kC$ over $H_d$, so its associated invertible module $\mathcal O(D_d)$ [def-pc-divisor-line-bundle] on $C_{H_d}=H_d\times_kC$ is defined;
2. the fibrewise degree of $\mathcal O(D_d)$ is $d$ at every point $t\in H_d$, so the class of $\mathcal O(D_d)$ is an element of $\operatorname{Pic}^d_{C/k}(H_d)$; let $\gamma_d:H_d\to P_d$ be the $k$-morphism corresponding to it under the representing isomorphism $\operatorname{Pic}^d_{C/k}\cong h_{P_d}$;
3. for every field extension $K/k$ [def-pc-field-extension] and every $K$-point $x:\operatorname{Spec}K\to H_d$, corresponding to a closed subscheme $D\subset C_K$ finite locally free of degree $d$ over $K$ (an effective Cartier divisor on $C_K$), the $K$-point $\gamma_d\circ x$ of $P_d$ corresponds to the class of $\mathcal O_{C_K}(D)$ in $\operatorname{Pic}^d_{C/k}(\operatorname{Spec}K)$.
